SECTION B — PRUNE TOWARD REAL MODULES  (Phase 1)
Collapse shim theater, kill import cycles. Mostly [P1], mostly quick/med.
============================================================

[x] Command package
	[x] [P1] (quick) collapse commands/ shims (registry, core, settings, __init__) into builtins+base
		-> builtins.py DELETED; each domain now owns its module; registry.py is the sole assembler
	[x] [P1] (med) stop builtins.py re-exporting from siblings; split by real domain instead
		[x] server / model / conversation / debug / permissions as own modules
		[x] also extracted core.py, tools.py, openrouter.py (were inline in builtins)
	[x] [P1] (med) break the builtins <-> debug/server circular mid-file imports
		-> HelpCommand now takes a registry callable; debug.py no longer imports builtins
	[x] [P1] (quick) add import-linter (or AST test) to forbid the cycle
		-> test/test_command_import_graph.py (AST-based, no new dependency)
	[ ] [P2] (med) replace 35 Command classes with a (name, desc, params, handler) registry
		[ ] keep classes only where subcommands + state are real (/server, /model, /debug)
		NOTE: deferred — the class hierarchy is now cheap to keep; revisit if it grows

[x] Input / completion
	[x] [P1] (med) merge 7 completion modules into one completion engine
		-> added completion.py (shared Completer base: suppression + menu lifecycle)
		-> command_/subcommand_/context_/argument_completion now subclass it
		-> DELETED path_completion.py + server_completion.py (303 lines, dead since
		   ArgumentCompletion replaced them — only mentioned in a docstring)
	[x] [P2] (med) audit coordinate_mapper / cursor_renderer / scroll_manager / input_handlers
		-> audit done: all four are live internals of input.py and directly
		   tested (test_basic_inputs, test_tui_interactions, test_buffer);
		   not vestigial, so no merge/deletion.

[x] Tools
	[x] [P1] (med) merge tools.py + tool_wrappers.py into one registry with a @tool decorator
		(name, schema, permission, settings) in one definition site
		-> tool_wrappers.py DELETED; tools.py now owns an @tool registry
		   (ToolDefinition/ToolContext/RegisteredTool). run is registered under
		   key run_command with LLM name run. Public factories (RunTool,
		   SearchWebTool, SearchWikiTool, SubagentTool, WaitForSubagentsTool)
		   kept for direct construction.

============================================================
SECTION C — UNIFY THE DOMAIN MODEL  (Phase 2, the core simplification)
The change that actually "simplifies the product". [P1], med/large.
============================================================

[x] Roles vs permission profiles — one model
	[x] [P1] (large) make Role the single source of truth (tools + policy + prompt)
		-> builtin/default/scaffolder roles are now constructed directly in
		   roles.py; no Role<->profile round-trip.
	[x] [P1] (med) demote tool_permissions to serialization/validation helpers only
		-> tool_permissions.py DELETED; low-level policy primitives now live in
		   the unified harness/permissions.py and are only execution helpers.
	[x] [P1] (med) delete Role.from_permission_profile / to_permission_profile translation layer
		-> both methods deleted. Tools/gate consume a Role or a low-level
		   profile through the adapters in permissions.py (file_permission,
		   resolve_run_permissions, search_permission).
	[x] [P1] (med) delete ui/profile_editor_model.py (keep role_editor_model as the one model)
		-> DELETED along with the /permissions profile subcommands and the
		   permission-profiles.toml store.
	[x] [P1] (med) collapse the two settings surfaces to one (settings tab + /permissions)
		-> /permissions now builds the same role fields as the settings tab via
		   settings_pages.build_roles_fields; build_permission_fields removed.
	[x] [P1] (quick) fix TODO complaints that fall out of this:
		[x] "role / permission is unclear"
		[x] "changing permission role: status bar not updated"
		[x] "deleting permission role not updated till input"

[x] Permissions — collapse four files into one question
	[x] [P1] (med) merge security.py + tool_permissions.py + permission_gate.py + role policy
		-> single "may I run this?" decision point (~1100 lines today)
		-> security.py + tool_permissions.py + permission_gate.py DELETED;
		   merged into harness/permissions.py (command checks, policy
		   primitives, PermissionGate). Gate now classifies commands with a
		   typed SecurityChecker.classify() instead of parsing messages.
	[ ] [P1] (med) retire the command allowlist as the security boundary
		-> DEFERRED BY DECISION: this pass unifies the code but keeps current
		   allowlist semantics so the permission suite stays valid.
		[ ] [P1] (quick) decide: container == allow, else ask
		[ ] [P2] (quick) delete CMD_DEFAULT_ALLOW / _ASK / _DENY + CMD_DANGEROUS_PATTERNS
		[ ] [P2] (quick) note: allowlist currently permits writes (cp/mv/mkdir/touch) and sed -i

